readonly tables: selectany so /ORDER can place them

Kind: link-layout stand-in (no compiler flag gives the same result).

The build places the readonly game pools with /ORDER
(layout/server.dll/common-data-order.txt; docs/msvc6-link-layout.md 30).
LINK puts ordered COMDATs before every ordinary .rdata contribution, so the
zlib tables that precede those pools in the reference must be COMDATs too.
MSVC 6 has no flag that makes data COMDAT (/Gy covers functions, /Gf and /GF
string literals), so each table becomes a selectany definition. Stock tables
with their /INCLUDE anchors removed keep every size but move readonly data
(10735 bytes differ); with no /ORDER at all 6324 bytes differ.

